+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are the `apiKeys`
+entries of the data file (`docs/DATA.md`); each has a role:
+
+- `viewer`: may only read (every `GET` route except `GET /audit`).
+- `cook`: also `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A route that is not a `GET` and is not marked for cooks in its route file
+needs a manager.
+
+No key or an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized` (also for routes that do
+not exist); a known key whose role is not enough answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request made with a known key that is not a `GET` writes an audit entry
+with its outcome, also when it was refused (403) or failed. Requests without
+a valid key (401) are not recorded. `GET /audit` (managers only) lists the
+entries newest first:
+
+    { "id": 3, "at": "2026-10-28T10:00:00.000Z", "keyName": "Seed cook",
+      "method": "POST", "path": "/recipes/1/cook", "status": 200 }
+
